== fuller page ==
Spread two said C4 asks for two ways to say everything. Here is how to tell
two ways from one way said twice: if either telling can be rebuilt from the
other, the pair has collapsed; "only one register is actually present, and
the second is decoration" [balance]. The shop's two tellings of a day's work
show the difference. Operational asks: did it hold, did it need rework, is
the box still up? Scientific asks: what was predicted, what was observed,
did the prediction survive? "Held" does not say whether holding was
expected, and a right forecast does not say whether anyone had to get up at
three in the morning [opsci].

Two writers is the same idea, for doing. "Load-bearing changes are built
twice, independently, and kept apart — agreement is evidence, disagreement
is information" [twice]. "A check run twice by one hand is one check"
[onehand]. When one experiment built its instrument twice, the two
disagreed once, and the disagreement was real: 68 = 4 × 17, and it
corrected the paper's first version [corrected].

The shop's tools carry it. tv1cr, which unfolds a table into folders,
writes every cell on both sides, in its row and in its column, "the two
writers", and its check reads each side against the other [writers].

So Spoke and Pin each write it down, apart. Same answer: good. Different
answer: good too, because now there is something to learn.

